# EnvironmentFile for pg-disk-hygiene.service and pg-worktree-sweep.service.
# Disk hygiene can read HOST_LINK_ID from the optional host-link.env loaded before this file.
# Operator step per host: mint an unscoped `sweep`-role token as a mode-0600 file at
# PG_TOKEN_FILE (`pg admin add-principal <name> --role sweep`), set PG_URL to the keeper API,
# and keep PG_SWEEP_CLAIMS_READER pointing at `plangraph.keeper.cli sweep-claims`.
PG_REPO=/home/USER/code/plangraph
PG_WORKTREES=/home/USER/code/plangraph-worktrees
PG_CLAUDE_WORKTREES=/home/USER/code/plangraph/.claude/worktrees
PG_RUNS=/home/USER/.local/state/plangraph/runs
PG_RUN_WORKTREES=/home/USER/.local/state/plangraph/worktrees
PG_PINS=/home/USER/.config/plangraph/pins.json
# If the spawner uses relocated run records or configured worktree mounts, set
# PLANGRAPH_SPAWN_STATE and PLANGRAPH_WORKTREE_MOUNTS to the same values here.
# Example for a workstation with worktree roots on all four WSL virtual disks:
# PLANGRAPH_WORKTREE_MOUNTS=/mnt/work-d:/mnt/work-f:/mnt/work-g:/mnt/work-h
PG_SWEEP_CLAIMS_READER="PYTHONPATH=/home/USER/code/plangraph/src /home/USER/code/plangraph/.venv/bin/python3 -m plangraph.keeper.cli sweep-claims"
PG_URL=https://KEEPER_HOST
PG_TOKEN_FILE=/home/USER/.config/plangraph/sweep.token
